-- title:
--   Polynomials in U preserve S and commute with Galois
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a commutative ring $O$ with an algebra structure $O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $h$, and a $p$-divisible group $H$ of height datum $(p,h)$ over $O$: a family of levels $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$, finite free cocommutative commutative Hopf $O$-algebras with $\operatorname{rank}_O H.\mathrm{level}\,v = p^{vh}$, together with surjective coalgebra maps $H.\mathrm{level}(v+1) \to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernels are the images of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. Let $u = (u_v)$ be a family of $O$-bialgebra endomorphisms of the levels, and let $U$ be a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear endomorphism of the Tate module $T = \mathrm{TateModule}\,p\,(H.\mathrm{Points}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, the group of sequences $x : \mathbb{N} \to H.\mathrm{Points}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, where $H.\mathrm{Points}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the direct limit of the additive groups of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $H.\mathrm{level}\,v \to_{\mathrm{alg}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ under convolution. Assume $U$ is induced by $u$ in the following pointwise sense: whenever a point $f$ at level $w$ represents the coordinate $x_n$, the coordinate $(Ux)_n$ is represented by $f \circ u_w$. Let $S \subseteq T$ be a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-submodule characterised by: $y \in S$ iff for every $n$ there are $w$ and a point $f$ at level $w$ representing $y_n$ with $P$-valuation of $f(a) - \varepsilon(a)$ less than $1$ for all $a \in H.\mathrm{level}\,w$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit followed by $O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then every $V$ in the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}_p}(T)$ generated by $U$ satisfies $V(S) \subseteq S$ and commutes with the Tate module action of every $\tau' \in \operatorname{Aut}_O \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. $\rho(\tau') \circ V = V \circ \rho(\tau')$.
--
--   This is the stability statement for the subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}_p[U] \subseteq \operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}_p}(T)$ attached to an endomorphism of a $p$-divisible group: the submodule $S$ of Tate sequences whose coordinates are represented by points congruent to the identity section at $P$ is preserved, and the Galois action is respected. It feeds the slope-type argument in which $U$ is decomposed by a unit-root idempotent, and is used in the derivation of the relation between the Tate module representation, the Frobenius–Verschiebung factorisation and the cyclotomic character.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_forall_mem_adjoin_tateModule_apply_mem_and_comp_tateModuleRep_eq.lean

